    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to make membership level 4 gated on tenure of more than 365 days, so a newly-created owner (zero tenure) never exceeds level 3.\n\nThe existing `AssignMembershipLevel` used a hard `Math.min(level, 3)` cap with a comment that level 4 was merely \"reserved for tenure\" \u2014 nothing actually implemented tenure. I replaced the arbitrary cap with a real tenure factor:\n\n**`AssignMembershipLevel.java`**\n- Level still starts at 1, +1 for an email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0` \u2014 so the creation-time factors naturally top out at 3.\n- Added a fourth increment when tenure (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())`) exceeds 365 days, and removed the `Math.min(..., 3)` cap so level 4 is now reachable \u2014 but only via tenure.\n- A new owner's `registrationDate` defaults to the server date (`BuildOwner`), giving zero tenure, so a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` 0, and a 3-member household lands at level 3, exactly as the spec and `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` require.\n\nNull `registrationDate` is treated as zero tenure defensively. The acceptance test and the full test suite both pass.",
